From 09ef52f275cd53144dd820a526ced0b2c14e7ccf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MicroNUX <micronux@example.invalid>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 00:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 30/48] video: fbdev: add ABI-v3 native cold probe

Select the display handoff ABI strictly from the device tree. Keep the
existing ABI-v2 loader-adoption path for M7, while M9 accepts only the
exact 192-byte ABI-v3 cold-relinquish contract.

Validate the immutable panel and memory profile, every cold-init MMIO
resource, silicon revision, reset and clock state, D-PHY LDO state, I2C
release, GDMA interrupt route, DMA PMS windows, no-map display pool, and
the dedicated cleared descriptor page outside the SD-DMA SRAM reserve,
without writing display hardware.

Stop M9 at an observable PROBED_QUIESCENT state. The adapter's ACKed
PWM-zero and reset commands are command-history facts, not optical-state
proof. Do not register framebuffer, backlight, touch input, or runtime IRQ
until later native initialization stages have succeeded.

Signed-off-by: MicroNUX <micronux@example.invalid>
---
 drivers/video/fbdev/esp32p4-dsi.c | 613 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 585 insertions(+), 28 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/video/fbdev/esp32p4-dsi.c b/drivers/video/fbdev/esp32p4-dsi.c
index 8154876..26f2c9a 100644
--- a/drivers/video/fbdev/esp32p4-dsi.c
+++ b/drivers/video/fbdev/esp32p4-dsi.c
@@ -2,16 +2,15 @@
 /*
  * ESP32-P4 MIPI-DSI ownership-transfer framebuffer for MicroNUX.
  *
- * The loader performs the panel-specific DBI sequence, leaves DPI mode active,
- * and publishes a bounded stopped DW-GDMA descriptor pool through a versioned
- * contract. This driver validates that contract, claims every persistent
- * controller resource, owns three framebuffers, and explicitly rearms one
- * complete-frame descriptor from each transfer-done interrupt. No loader
- * callback remains live.
+ * ABI v2 adopts a loader-initialized display for M7. ABI v3 strictly validates
+ * an M9 cold-relinquish contract and quiescent hardware state before native
+ * Linux initialization. The required ABI comes from the device tree; the two
+ * modes are never selected by probing live hardware or by fallback.
  */
 
 #include <linux/backlight.h>
 #include <linux/bitops.h>
+#include <linux/build_bug.h>
 #include <linux/crc32.h>
 #include <linux/delay.h>
 #include <linux/fb.h>
@@ -32,10 +31,17 @@
